Chapter: ListPrim2False

 The guard on the three later reduction rules
 (list-set-at, list-insert-at, and & append over Nil/Cons spines). Each
 claim below states the wrong value for a shape whose rule does fire,
 so each must be a hard CDX2001 naming the reduced term. If this file
 ever compiles, a rule folded to something the runtime never produces,
 or the unifier admitted Refl against a stuck spine.

Section: Claims

  claim bad-set : list-set-at (Cons 5 (Cons 6 Nil)) 0 9 === Cons 5 (Cons 9 Nil)
  proof bad-set = Refl
  qed

  claim bad-insert : list-insert-at (Cons 5 Nil) 0 9 === Cons 5 (Cons 9 Nil)
  proof bad-insert = Refl
  qed

  claim bad-append : Cons 1 Nil & Cons 2 Nil === Cons 2 (Cons 1 Nil)
  proof bad-append = Refl
  qed

Section: Main

  opening : [Console] Nothing
  opening = act
   print-line-uni "list-prim2-false: should not compile"
  end
